1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,710
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,710 --> 00:00:04,940
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:06,090
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,090 --> 00:00:07,000
I had my right knee

5
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,660
replaced two years ago.

6
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:10,460
It has hurt every day
since.

7
00:00:10,460 --> 00:00:11,800
Not surgery pain.

8
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:12,960
I know what that felt
like,

9
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:13,820
and it went away.

10
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:15,070
This is different.

11
00:00:15,070 --> 00:00:15,892
Tight.

12
00:00:15,892 --> 00:00:16,780
Full.

13
00:00:16,780 --> 00:00:17,670
Like a band around

14
00:00:17,670 --> 00:00:19,710
the joint that never
loosens.

15
00:00:19,710 --> 00:00:20,810
And for two years

16
00:00:20,810 --> 00:00:22,630
I've been told the same
thing.

17
00:00:22,630 --> 00:00:23,740
Give it time.

18
00:00:23,740 --> 00:00:25,390
At six weeks it was
swelling,

19
00:00:25,390 --> 00:00:26,746
and swelling is normal.

20
00:00:26,746 --> 00:00:27,510
At three months,

21
00:00:27,510 --> 00:00:28,820
give it six.

22
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:30,001
At six months,

23
00:00:30,001 --> 00:00:32,060
some knees take a full
year.

24
00:00:32,060 --> 00:00:32,920
At a year,

25
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:35,200
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

26
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,250
And I didn't just wait.

27
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:37,660
We went down the list.

28
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:39,200
More physical therapy.

29
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,090
Every session,

30
00:00:40,090 --> 00:00:41,670
every exercise at home.

31
00:00:41,670 --> 00:00:42,713
I got stronger.

32
00:00:42,713 --> 00:00:44,360
The tightness never moved.

33
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:45,840
The pain pills helped,

34
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:47,240
and that was the problem.

35
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:48,840
I'm already on enough
every morning,

36
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:49,880
and nobody could tell me

37
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:51,460
when I'd get to stop.

38
00:00:51,460 --> 00:00:52,885
Then a nerve block.

39
00:00:52,885 --> 00:00:54,760
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

40
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:56,320
And after that, a second

41
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:57,580
operation to go back

42
00:00:57,580 --> 00:00:59,390
in and do it over.

43
00:00:59,390 --> 00:01:00,700
I said no.

44
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:02,370
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

45
00:01:02,370 --> 00:01:03,270
and my knee felt like

46
00:01:03,270 --> 00:01:05,210
a band was wrapped around
it,

47
00:01:05,210 --> 00:01:07,580
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

48
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:08,850
Every morning I took
something

49
00:01:08,850 --> 00:01:09,590
for it and got

50
00:01:09,590 --> 00:01:10,810
on with my day.

51
00:01:10,810 --> 00:01:12,560
Couldn't do the stairs,

52
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:13,770
couldn't stand at the
counter

53
00:01:13,770 --> 00:01:15,540
long enough to finish
dinner,

54
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:17,080
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

55
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:19,400
game without shifting
every two minutes.

56
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:20,920
It woke me at night,

57
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:22,860
and it turned ordinary
things,

58
00:01:22,860 --> 00:01:24,060
like getting in the car

59
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:25,580
or up off the couch,

60
00:01:25,580 --> 00:01:26,980
into a decision.

61
00:01:26,980 --> 00:01:28,330
After a long and serious

62
00:01:28,330 --> 00:01:29,630
talk with my wife,

63
00:01:29,630 --> 00:01:31,700
I went back in one more
time.

64
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:32,840
That was the fourth set

65
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:34,520
of X-rays on this knee.

66
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:36,240
And like the three before
it,

67
00:01:36,240 --> 00:01:39,010
the answer was everything
looks great.

68
00:01:39,010 --> 00:01:41,120
No loosening, no
infection,

69
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:42,460
nothing wrong.

70
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:43,380
Only this time there

71
00:01:43,380 --> 00:01:44,670
was no new number.

72
00:01:44,670 --> 00:01:45,370
Nobody said

73
00:01:45,370 --> 00:01:46,898
give it another six
months.

74
00:01:46,898 --> 00:01:48,970
There was nothing left to
give it.

75
00:01:48,970 --> 00:01:50,310
I sat in the parking

76
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:51,700
lot for a while.

77
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:53,620
Okay, I thought.

78
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:55,280
Then explain this.

79
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:57,080
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

80
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:58,860
I hit my breaking point.

81
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:01,110
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

82
00:02:01,110 --> 00:02:02,890
Everyone in the house was
asleep

83
00:02:02,890 --> 00:02:04,510
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

84
00:02:04,510 --> 00:02:05,530
with my leg up,

85
00:02:05,530 --> 00:02:07,400
trying to find any angle
where

86
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:08,590
it didn't feel like
something

87
00:02:08,590 --> 00:02:10,250
was wrapped around my knee

88
00:02:10,250 --> 00:02:11,290
and tightening.

89
00:02:11,290 --> 00:02:13,810
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

90
00:02:13,810 --> 00:02:15,870
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

91
00:02:15,870 --> 00:02:16,920
And I just thought,

92
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:18,560
is this really my life
now?

93
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:20,160
I can't live like this.

94
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:22,480
So I made myself a
promise.

95
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:23,320
I wouldn't go a day

96
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:25,030
without looking for an
answer.

97
00:02:25,030 --> 00:02:26,480
And when I found one,

98
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:27,450
I'd share it with everyone

99
00:02:27,450 --> 00:02:29,270
going through the same
thing.

100
00:02:29,270 --> 00:02:30,200
So I got my laptop

101
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:31,770
out and went looking.

102
00:02:31,770 --> 00:02:32,930
Not for a product.

103
00:02:32,930 --> 00:02:34,250
For an explanation.

104
00:02:34,250 --> 00:02:35,840
Mayo Clinic forums,

105
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:38,120
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

106
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:40,755
doctor videos, medical
animations.

107
00:02:40,755 --> 00:02:41,660
And that's when I found

108
00:02:41,660 --> 00:02:43,200
a video from a physical
therapist

109
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:43,680
named Dr.

110
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:45,710
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

111
00:02:45,710 --> 00:02:47,659
had been through exactly
this.

112
00:02:47,659 --> 00:02:49,950
But before I say anything
else,

113
00:02:49,950 --> 00:02:51,780
I want to be straight with
you.

114
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:54,250
You've already had
something work fast.

115
00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:55,226
The ice.

116
00:02:55,226 --> 00:02:57,055
The first week of a new
pill.

117
00:02:57,055 --> 00:02:58,978
The good day after a
session.

118
00:02:58,978 --> 00:03:00,651
Then it wore off.

119
00:03:00,651 --> 00:03:03,123
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

120
00:03:03,123 --> 00:03:04,770
Fast relief isn't relief.

121
00:03:04,770 --> 00:03:05,965
It's a preview.

122
00:03:05,965 --> 00:03:07,310
So I'm not going to tell

123
00:03:07,310 --> 00:03:09,150
you this works fast.

124
00:03:09,150 --> 00:03:10,043
It doesn't.

125
00:03:10,043 --> 00:03:11,910
But if you're willing to
be patient,

126
00:03:11,910 --> 00:03:12,830
and to look at what's

127
00:03:12,830 --> 00:03:14,360
going on around your new
knee

128
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:16,110
instead of inside it,
there

129
00:03:16,110 --> 00:03:18,651
is a real reason it still
hurts.

130
00:03:18,651 --> 00:03:20,920
And something you can do
about it.

131
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:22,130
Let me explain what he
said,

132
00:03:22,130 --> 00:03:23,590
because this is what
changed

133
00:03:23,590 --> 00:03:24,810
everything for me.

134
00:03:24,810 --> 00:03:26,680
He started with the
basics.

135
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:28,150
A knee replacement takes
out

136
00:03:28,150 --> 00:03:30,540
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

137
00:03:30,540 --> 00:03:32,370
in metal and plastic.

138
00:03:32,370 --> 00:03:34,650
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

139
00:03:34,650 --> 00:03:36,749
you had before the
operation.

140
00:03:36,749 --> 00:03:38,720
That part I already knew.

141
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:40,240
But then he explained
something

142
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:41,790
nobody had ever told me.

143
00:03:41,790 --> 00:03:42,698
He said,

144
00:03:42,698 --> 00:03:44,240
think about a swollen foot

145
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:45,500
inside a shoe.

146
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:47,070
The shoe didn't shrink.

147
00:03:47,070 --> 00:03:49,537
Your foot is taking up
more room,

148
00:03:49,537 --> 00:03:51,280
so everything feels
cramped

149
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:53,390
and tight and squeezed.

150
00:03:53,390 --> 00:03:54,650
Your new knee sits

151
00:03:54,650 --> 00:03:56,320
in a limited space with
living

152
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:58,520
tissue packed all around
it.

153
00:03:58,520 --> 00:04:00,530
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

154
00:04:00,530 --> 00:04:02,500
had to work through that
tissue.

155
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:05,300
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

156
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:06,880
At first that's normal.

157
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:08,430
But in some people that
swelling can

158
00:04:08,430 --> 00:04:11,410
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

159
00:04:11,410 --> 00:04:13,080
And swollen tissue takes
up more

160
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:15,090
room than calm tissue
does.

161
00:04:15,090 --> 00:04:16,360
So when you bend,

162
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:18,310
that tissue gets
compressed.

163
00:04:18,310 --> 00:04:19,470
When you straighten,

164
00:04:19,470 --> 00:04:21,060
it gets pulled tight.

165
00:04:21,060 --> 00:04:22,250
That's the band.

166
00:04:22,250 --> 00:04:25,380
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

167
00:04:25,380 --> 00:04:26,220
And you start being

168
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:27,050
the one who says,

169
00:04:27,050 --> 00:04:28,190
you go ahead.

170
00:04:28,190 --> 00:04:29,590
I'll stay here.

171
00:04:29,590 --> 00:04:31,340
And that's exactly why so
much

172
00:04:31,340 --> 00:04:33,333
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

173
00:04:33,333 --> 00:04:35,250
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

174
00:04:35,250 --> 00:04:36,400
around the knee.

175
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:37,120
Worth doing,

176
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:38,360
and I'd done it.

177
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:39,660
It does nothing about
tissue

178
00:04:39,660 --> 00:04:40,700
taking up room.

179
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:41,880
A nerve block quiets

180
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:43,770
the nerve carrying the
signal.

181
00:04:43,770 --> 00:04:46,611
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

182
00:04:46,611 --> 00:04:48,210
But when that irritated
tissue

183
00:04:48,210 --> 00:04:49,820
finally calms down,

184
00:04:49,820 --> 00:04:51,580
it holds less fluid,

185
00:04:51,580 --> 00:04:53,440
and it takes up less room.

186
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:54,740
Less room taken up means

187
00:04:54,740 --> 00:04:57,041
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

188
00:04:57,041 --> 00:04:59,140
That's what takes the
pressure off.

189
00:04:59,140 --> 00:05:00,630
After two years of this,

190
00:05:00,630 --> 00:05:02,560
it finally made sense.

191
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:04,600
The problem was never the
new knee.

192
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:06,841
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

193
00:05:06,841 --> 00:05:08,514
He calls it the squeeze.

194
00:05:08,514 --> 00:05:11,150
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

195
00:05:11,150 --> 00:05:12,620
I'd bought knee sleeves,

196
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:14,900
compression braces,
creams,

197
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:16,700
half of Amazon really,

198
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:18,110
and all any of it gave me

199
00:05:18,110 --> 00:05:19,330
was an hour.

200
00:05:19,330 --> 00:05:20,400
I even looked at going

201
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:22,368
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

202
00:05:22,368 --> 00:05:24,420
But at $200 a session

203
00:05:24,420 --> 00:05:26,366
with nothing covered by
insurance,

204
00:05:26,366 --> 00:05:27,590
that was a quick no.

205
00:05:27,590 --> 00:05:28,640
Then one night I went

206
00:05:28,640 --> 00:05:29,910
back to that knee
replacement

207
00:05:29,910 --> 00:05:31,650
group and actually read
it.

208
00:05:31,650 --> 00:05:32,960
Thousands of people,

209
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:34,598
years out from surgery,

210
00:05:34,598 --> 00:05:36,880
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

211
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:38,623
nobody could explain.

212
00:05:38,623 --> 00:05:40,320
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

213
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:42,040
the same thing kept coming
up.

214
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:44,090
This one device,

215
00:05:44,090 --> 00:05:45,600
and people saying it was
the first

216
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:47,290
thing that made a
difference.

217
00:05:47,290 --> 00:05:49,502
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

218
00:05:49,502 --> 00:05:50,790
alright, here it comes,

219
00:05:50,790 --> 00:05:52,130
he's selling me something,

220
00:05:52,130 --> 00:05:53,950
let me shut that down
right now.

221
00:05:53,950 --> 00:05:55,440
I'm only here because I
made myself

222
00:05:55,440 --> 00:05:57,460
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

223
00:05:57,460 --> 00:05:58,370
that if I ever found

224
00:05:58,370 --> 00:05:59,500
something that helped,

225
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:01,100
I'd say so.

226
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:02,860
It's called the KenRelief
Red

227
00:06:02,860 --> 00:06:04,480
Light Therapy Wrap.

228
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:06,570
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

229
00:06:06,570 --> 00:06:07,670
It looked like the cheap

230
00:06:07,670 --> 00:06:09,450
knee sleeves off Amazon

231
00:06:09,450 --> 00:06:11,182
that did nothing for me.

232
00:06:11,182 --> 00:06:13,140
But I went to their
website anyway,

233
00:06:13,140 --> 00:06:14,050
just to see what all

234
00:06:14,050 --> 00:06:15,440
the fuss was about.

235
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:17,040
It's the same red light
therapy

236
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:19,250
clinics charge $200 a
session

237
00:06:19,250 --> 00:06:21,380
for, off machines that
cost

238
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:22,890
fifty thousand dollars,

239
00:06:22,890 --> 00:06:23,960
in a wrap you plug

240
00:06:23,960 --> 00:06:25,440
into the wall at home.

241
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:27,260
Two hundred and forty
lights.

242
00:06:27,260 --> 00:06:29,750
Red at 660 nanometers

243
00:06:29,750 --> 00:06:32,400
and near-infrared at 850,

244
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:34,896
run together for the
strongest effect.

245
00:06:34,896 --> 00:06:36,480
Four strength levels.

246
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:38,400
A five to thirty minute
timer.

247
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:39,970
Then I saw the guarantee.

248
00:06:39,970 --> 00:06:41,210
Ninety days.

249
00:06:41,210 --> 00:06:43,080
Results or your money
back,

250
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:45,630
no questions, no store
credit,

251
00:06:45,630 --> 00:06:47,590
and you don't even send it
back.

252
00:06:47,590 --> 00:06:50,010
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

253
00:06:50,010 --> 00:06:51,740
days to change my mind.

254
00:06:51,740 --> 00:06:53,180
There wasn't much to lose,

255
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:54,230
so I ordered it.

256
00:06:54,230 --> 00:06:55,650
Two of them, actually.

257
00:06:55,650 --> 00:06:57,740
Only the right knee was
replaced,

258
00:06:57,740 --> 00:06:59,870
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

259
00:06:59,870 --> 00:07:01,560
and I'd done it for two
years.

260
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:03,700
The left one was carrying
the difference.

261
00:07:03,700 --> 00:07:04,310
When it came,

262
00:07:04,310 --> 00:07:06,320
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

263
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:07,610
because I'd been let down
too

264
00:07:07,610 --> 00:07:09,480
many times to get excited.

265
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:11,470
What I felt was warmth.

266
00:07:11,470 --> 00:07:13,570
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

267
00:07:13,570 --> 00:07:15,340
More like it was coming
from inside

268
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:17,340
the knee and spreading
around it.

269
00:07:17,340 --> 00:07:18,320
And that was it.

270
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:20,068
That was the whole
experience.

271
00:07:20,068 --> 00:07:21,130
When I took it off,

272
00:07:21,130 --> 00:07:22,230
I'll be honest,

273
00:07:22,230 --> 00:07:24,220
nothing dramatic had
happened.

274
00:07:24,220 --> 00:07:25,640
And after what that video
said,

275
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:27,620
that's exactly what I
expected.

276
00:07:27,620 --> 00:07:28,360
What was different

277
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:29,730
was that for the first

278
00:07:29,730 --> 00:07:31,050
time in two years

279
00:07:31,050 --> 00:07:32,750
I'd done something for my
knee

280
00:07:32,750 --> 00:07:34,071
instead of to it.

281
00:07:34,071 --> 00:07:35,060
Twenty minutes,

282
00:07:35,060 --> 00:07:36,230
in my own chair.

283
00:07:36,230 --> 00:07:37,950
No drive, no copay.

284
00:07:37,950 --> 00:07:39,530
They say twenty minutes.

285
00:07:39,530 --> 00:07:40,770
I did thirty,

286
00:07:40,770 --> 00:07:41,920
twice a day,

287
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:44,030
lowest setting that first
week.

288
00:07:44,030 --> 00:07:45,661
I put it on the calendar.

289
00:07:45,661 --> 00:07:46,400
The first week,

290
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:47,170
I couldn't have told

291
00:07:47,170 --> 00:07:48,920
you if anything was
happening.

292
00:07:48,920 --> 00:07:49,730
I tried not to get

293
00:07:49,730 --> 00:07:50,820
my hopes up.

294
00:07:50,820 --> 00:07:52,457
I'd had things help for a
week

295
00:07:52,457 --> 00:07:53,670
and then stop.

296
00:07:53,670 --> 00:07:55,030
But somewhere in the
second week

297
00:07:55,030 --> 00:07:56,130
I noticed I'd come down

298
00:07:56,130 --> 00:07:58,000
the stairs without holding
the rail.

299
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,470
I hadn't decided to.

300
00:07:59,470 --> 00:08:00,532
I just did it,

301
00:08:00,532 --> 00:08:01,770
then stopped halfway down

302
00:08:01,770 --> 00:08:03,320
because I realized.

303
00:08:03,320 --> 00:08:04,840
By the end of the fourth
week

304
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:06,050
I'd slept through the
night

305
00:08:06,050 --> 00:08:07,710
four times running.

306
00:08:07,710 --> 00:08:08,720
I stood at the counter

307
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:09,850
and finished making dinner

308
00:08:09,850 --> 00:08:11,760
without looking for the
stool.

309
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:13,400
None of that is dramatic.

310
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:14,430
All of it was gone

311
00:08:14,430 --> 00:08:15,860
for two years.

312
00:08:15,860 --> 00:08:17,450
A few weeks later my wife
asked

313
00:08:17,450 --> 00:08:18,280
if I wanted to walk

314
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:19,918
the long way around the
block.

315
00:08:19,918 --> 00:08:20,810
And for the first time

316
00:08:20,810 --> 00:08:21,480
in two years,

317
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:22,810
I said yes.

318
00:08:22,810 --> 00:08:24,538
I wanted to understand
why,

319
00:08:24,538 --> 00:08:26,220
so I read the whole thing.

320
00:08:26,220 --> 00:08:27,960
It comes down to four
steps.

321
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:28,940
One.

322
00:08:28,940 --> 00:08:30,460
The tissue around a new
knee can

323
00:08:30,460 --> 00:08:33,230
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

324
00:08:33,230 --> 00:08:33,860
Two.

325
00:08:33,860 --> 00:08:36,164
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

326
00:08:36,164 --> 00:08:37,070
so it takes up more

327
00:08:37,070 --> 00:08:38,197
room than it should.

328
00:08:38,197 --> 00:08:39,067
Three.

329
00:08:39,067 --> 00:08:40,940
There's only so much room
in there.

330
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:42,718
Bending compresses it.

331
00:08:42,718 --> 00:08:44,520
Straightening pulls it
tight.

332
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:45,965
That's the squeeze.

333
00:08:45,965 --> 00:08:47,070
Four.

334
00:08:47,070 --> 00:08:48,850
Red and near-infrared
light have been

335
00:08:48,850 --> 00:08:50,960
studied for calming that
inflammation,

336
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:52,240
so the swelling and the
pressure

337
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:53,700
can come down with it.

338
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:55,490
In a randomized trial,

339
00:08:55,490 --> 00:08:57,620
patients given light
therapy after

340
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:58,660
a knee replacement

341
00:08:58,660 --> 00:09:00,070
had less pain,

342
00:09:00,070 --> 00:09:00,870
less swelling

343
00:09:00,870 --> 00:09:02,830
and better early movement
than

344
00:09:02,830 --> 00:09:04,190
those who weren't.

345
00:09:04,190 --> 00:09:07,090
A 2025 review said the
same,

346
00:09:07,090 --> 00:09:08,350
and was clear the evidence

347
00:09:08,350 --> 00:09:09,510
is still limited.

348
00:09:09,510 --> 00:09:11,230
I probably sound like a
broken

349
00:09:11,230 --> 00:09:12,933
record to my family.

350
00:09:12,933 --> 00:09:15,220
But after two years of
doing everything

351
00:09:15,220 --> 00:09:17,640
I was told and getting
nowhere,

352
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:19,040
you have no idea what it's

353
00:09:19,040 --> 00:09:20,526
like to sleep through the
night,

354
00:09:20,526 --> 00:09:22,220
say yes to the walk,

355
00:09:22,220 --> 00:09:24,380
and get my life back.

356
00:09:24,380 --> 00:09:25,780
So take it from me.

357
00:09:25,780 --> 00:09:27,300
Don't spend another year
waiting

358
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:28,530
for it to settle.

359
00:09:28,530 --> 00:09:30,600
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

360
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:32,090
More than ten thousand
people

361
00:09:32,090 --> 00:09:33,130
with pain after a knee

362
00:09:33,130 --> 00:09:35,200
replacement have already
tried this.

363
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:37,160
Some had it worse than I
did.

364
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:38,340
You can get the KenRelief

365
00:09:38,340 --> 00:09:40,064
wrap from their website,

366
00:09:40,064 --> 00:09:41,630
